{"path":"atomic/atomic/fetch_min","title":"std::atomic<T>::fetch_min","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::atomic&lt;T&gt;::</span>fetch_min","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic/fetch_min","section":"atomic","kind":"page","summary":"Atomically replaces the current value with the result of std::min of the value and arg. That is, it performs atomic minimum operation.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div>member only of <code>atomic&lt;<i>Integral</i></code> ﻿<code>&gt;</code> specializations</div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T fetch_min<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T arg, <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T fetch_min<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T arg, <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div>member only of <code>atomic&lt;T*&gt;</code> partial specialization</div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> fetch_min<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> arg, <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> fetch_min<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> arg, <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Atomically replaces the current value with the result of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/min\">std::min</a></span> of the value and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">arg</span></code>. That is, it performs atomic minimum operation. The operation is a read-modify-write operation. Memory is affected according to the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3,4)</span> If the pointers point to different complete objects (or subobjects thereof), <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/operator_comparison#Built-in_pointer_relational_comparison\">pointer comparison</a> does not establish a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/strict_weak_ordering\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">strict weak ordering</a>.</div>\n<p>It is deprecated if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic\"><span class=\"kw2083\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_always_lock_free</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> and overload <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span> or <span class=\"t-v\">(4)</span> participates in overload resolution.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> arg\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the other argument of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/min\">std::min</a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> order\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> memory order constraints to enforce\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The value immediately preceding the effects of this function in the <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order#Modification_order\">modification order</a> of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_atomic_min_max\"><code>__cpp_lib_atomic_min_max</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/26#cpp_lib_atomic_min_max_202403L\"><code>202403L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++26)</span></td>\n<td>Atomic minimum/maximum\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"atomic","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"atomic/atomic","title":"std::atomic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::atomic<T>::fetch_min","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++26. Atomically replaces the current value with the result of std::min of the value and arg."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"arg, order"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The value immediately preceding the effects of this function in the modification order of *this."},{"label":"Notes"},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":190,"codeBlockCount":0}
